{"repositoryId":1047420836,"availability":"available","full":"Zheruel/nano-string-utils","name":"nano-string-utils","description":"61 zero-dependency string utilities for TypeScript and JavaScript. Tree-shakeable, under 1 KB each — camelCase, slugify, validation, XSS sanitization, fuzzy matching, Unicode.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":82,"forks":9,"created":"2025-08-30T11:37:24Z","updated":"2026-09-07T19:25:12Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://zheruel.github.io/nano-string-utils/","topics":["bun","camelcase","cjs","deno","es-toolkit","esm","javascript","lightweight","lodash-alternative","npm-package","slugify","string-manipulation","string-utils","string-validation","text-processing","tree-shakeable","typescript","typescript-library","utilities","zero-dependencies"],"demo":"https://zheruel.github.io/nano-string-utils/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.680Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.680Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.680Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.680Z","stars":82,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["61 string utilities for TypeScript and JavaScript.","Zero dependencies, tree-shakeable, under 1 KB each.","nano-string-utils is a modern string utility library for JavaScript and TypeScript: case conversion (camelCase, kebabCase, snakecase, PascalCase), slugify, truncate, email and URL validation, HTML escaping and XSS sanitization, fuzzy matching, Levenshtein distance, pluralization, Unicode and emoji-safe helpers, and more. It has no runtime dependencies, ships ESM and CommonJS, and every function is independently importable — so a lodash or underscore.string replacement costs you bytes, not kilobytes."],"features":["Nothing you didn't ask for. Zero runtime dependencies means zero transitive supply-chain surface. The whole library is 9.6 KB brotlied; a typical import is a few hundred bytes.","Real tree-shaking. Every function lives in its own module and is marked side-effect free, so bundlers drop what you don't reference.","Types that do work. Branded types make a validated Email or URL unforgeable, and template literal types compute exact return values at compile time.","Null-safe by default. Almost every function takes null or undefined and passes it straight through instead of throwing. See Null safety for the four that don't.","Unicode-aware where it counts. graphemes, codePoints, reverse, and toASCII handle emoji, combining marks, and surrogate pairs correctly."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zheruel/nano-string-utils/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"59e666de5a3401eca192385550f2044b39bd08b3d9e076da2106d7cf2ccc0ddd","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.802Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.802Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"61 string utilities for TypeScript and JavaScript.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zheruel/nano-string-utils/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"59e666de5a3401eca192385550f2044b39bd08b3d9e076da2106d7cf2ccc0ddd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zheruel/nano-string-utils/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.802Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-07T19:25:12Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Zheruel/nano-string-utils/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.803Z","hash":"59e666de5a3401eca192385550f2044b39bd08b3d9e076da2106d7cf2ccc0ddd","originalBytes":22835,"storedBytes":22835,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["function","string","nano-string-utils","npm","run","lodash","null","email","input","camelcase","es-toolkit","gzipped","slugify","convert","every","case","hello-world","nano-string","template","const","hello","truncate","type","what","add","characters","deno","does","install","isemail","length","text","types","typescript","bytes","functions","html","import","library","only","world","